t%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":36077475,"digest":"sha256:3d4078829375b8b8d0dbd76490f7130d9023bd08fc2e55a2cf9f68768448b1e8","download_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-04T09:48:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T09:48:54Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/typeward/typeward/releases/download/v0.1.0/Typeward_x86_64-apple-darwin.app.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeward/typeward/tarball/v0.1.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeward/typeward/zipball/v0.1.0","body":"## Typeward 0.1.0, the first public beta (2026-09-04)\n\nTypeward is a LaTeX and Typst editor that runs entirely on your machine. There\nis no account to create, nothing to subscribe to, and no server holding your\nwork. Projects are ordinary folders on your disk that you can back up, version,\nand open with any other tool. Third-party integrations (Zotero, Mendeley,\nWebDAV, git remotes, AI providers) are optional and use your own credentials.\n\n**This is a first beta.** It is the first build published outside the\nmaintainer machine it was developed on, so expect rough edges on other setups.\nPlease open an issue for anything you hit.\n\n### Install\n\n| System | Architecture | Download |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Windows 10 and 11 | x86_64 | `Typeward_0.1.0_x64-setup.exe` |\n| Windows 10 and 11 | ARM64 | `Typeward_0.1.0_arm64-setup.exe` |\n| macOS 13.3 or newer | Apple Silicon | `Typeward_0.1.0_aarch64.dmg` |\n| macOS 13.3 or newer | Intel | `Typeward_0.1.0_x64.dmg` |\n| Linux, glibc 2.35+ | x86_64 | `Typeward_0.1.0_amd64.deb`, `Typeward-0.1.0-1.x86_64.rpm`, `Typeward_0.1.0_amd64.AppImage` |\n| Linux, glibc 2.35+ | ARM64 | `Typeward_0.1.0_arm64.deb`, `Typeward-0.1.0-1.aarch64.rpm`, `Typeward_0.1.0_aarch64.AppImage` |\n\nLinux is one build per architecture rather than one per distribution. The `.deb`\ncovers the Debian family (Debian 12+, Ubuntu 22.04+, Mint, Pop!_OS, elementary),\nthe `.rpm` covers the RPM family (Fedora 36+, openSUSE, the RHEL derivatives),\nand the AppImage runs on anything else at or above that glibc level, Arch and\nother rolling releases included.\n\nWindows needs the WebView2 runtime. It is preinstalled on Windows 11 and\ninstalled on demand elsewhere.\n\n### These installers are not code-signed\n\nCode signing certificates are not in place yet, so the operating system will\nwarn you:\n\n- **Windows:** SmartScreen shows \"Windows protected your PC\". Choose \"More info\",\n  then \"Run anyway\".\n- **macOS:** Gatekeeper refuses to open the app on first launch. Right-click the\n  app in Applications and choose \"Open\", or clear the quarantine flag with\n  `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Typeward.app`. On recent macOS\n  you may instead need System Settings > Privacy & Security > \"Open Anyway\".\n- **Linux:** no OS signing story applies. Integrity rides on the checksums below.\n\nVerify the download before you run it. That is the real integrity check here,\nand it is stronger than a signature you cannot inspect.\n\nNote that this is about *OS code signing* only. The auto-updater is a separate\nmechanism and it is fully signed: every platform entry in `latest.json` carries\na real updater signature, and the updater verifies each download against the\npublic key compiled into the app.\n\n### Compile engines are user-installed\n\nTeX distributions, Typst, and pandoc are detected on your PATH rather than\nbundled, so Typeward uses whatever you already have. Tectonic is the one\nexception: it ships inside the app on Windows x86_64, Linux x86_64, and both\nmacOS builds, so a LaTeX project compiles out of the box there.\n\nThe **Windows ARM64 and Linux ARM64 builds do not carry Tectonic**, because\nupstream publishes no aarch64 Windows binary. LaTeX on those two needs a TeX\ndistribution or a `tectonic` you install yourself. Typst is unaffected.\n\n### Verify your download\n\n```\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing\n```\n\nBuild provenance: `gh attestation verify <file> --repo typeward/typeward`\n\n### License\n\nMIT with the Commons Clause. Source available, and free for any use including\ncommercial work, but not for selling Typeward itself. See `LICENSE`.\n\n"}]